  {
   "id": 516608,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<b>Percent Error.</b> When performing a scientific experiment that results in quantities of some sort, such as mass in chemistry or momentum in physics, the percent error is often computed. Percent error, %<span data-math=\"E\">E</span>, is the percent by which the value obtained in an experiment, the observed value <span data-math=\"O\">O</span>, is different than the value that was expected, the expected value <span data-math=\"E\">E</span>, in the experiment. The formula is below.<br>\n<span data-math=\"\\% E = \\frac{{|O - E|}}{E}\">\\% E = \\frac{{|O - E|}}{E}</span><br>\nJim and Kelly are working on a chemistry experiment and expect the result to be 50 grams. However, their result was 48.7 grams. Find Jim and Kelly’s percent error.",
